### A.4 Critical notes on individual species

**R. gallica.** The tetraploid assembly is fragmented (>3,514 contigs) and the reported SER for A13 is 3.27%. The pangenome reports BUSCO completeness of 94.2% for polyploid accessions and an average contig N50 of 29.2 Mb across assemblies, but the *R. gallica* assembly specifically has been flagged as problematic. This is above the 2% threshold for full tetraploid HMM application and requires the simplification rule (fix \(c_i\) from cytogenetics) to be activated. Under the pre-registered F6 threshold (chromosome-level assembly, BUSCO > 90%), *R. gallica* is **PROVISIONAL**. If it fails F6 after further assembly refinement, the candidate set collapses to *R. moschata* and *R. fedtschenkoana*—a scenario that would require the thesis to formally test whether a bipartite model plus ghost introgression explains the data.

**R. fedtschenkoana.** A high-quality chromosome-level assembly is now available: total assembly size of 547.5 Mb, contig N50 of 73.5 Mb, BUSCO completeness of 97.36%, and 95.72% of the assembly anchored to seven pseudochromosomes. This substantially de-risks this lineage and it passes F6.

**R. majalis.** Available resources are limited to Illumina genome skims (18.9 Gb of raw data from a single HiSeq 2500 run) and chloroplast sequences (157,258 bp). No chromosome-level assembly exists. This lineage fails F6.

**R. davurica.** Available resources are limited to a single chloroplast genome sequence (156 kb, accession MW381769) and resequencing data for genetic background analysis. No chromosome-level assembly exists. This lineage fails F6.

**R. moschata.** Part of the 2026 pangenome; presumed chromosome-level and passing F6, though specific assembly metrics remain to be documented in the final audit.

