## Appendix D: ABC-RF Scenario Comparison Protocol

### D.1 Purpose

This appendix specifies the ABC-random forest protocol for scenario comparison described in Chapter 6. ABC-RF is a supervised machine-learning approach for model choice and parameter inference. It can be used for model selection, parameter estimation within a model, and estimation of posterior probabilities. ABC-RF is robust to the inclusion of poorly informative or irrelevant summary statistics.

### D.2 Scenario definitions

| Scenario | Description | Processes |
|---|---|---|
| \(S_1\) | Hybridization only | Ancient multi-parental mosaic |
| \(S_2\) | Hybridization + introgression | Initial hybridization followed by gene flow |
| \(S_3\) | ILS-dominated | Ancestral polymorphism; no recent gene flow |
| \(S_4\) | Hybridization + introgression + ghost | Ghost lineage contributes to focal and donor |

**Critical note on scenario composability:** The scenarios are not mutually exclusive biological hypotheses. They represent different **compositions of processes**. \(S_4\) includes all processes in \(S_2\) plus ghost ancestry. The comparison asks which composition of processes best explains the data, not which single process is the sole cause of all discordance. This reflects the biological reality that hybridization, introgression, incomplete lineage sorting, and ghost ancestry can coexist.

### D.3 Pre-registered priors

| Parameter | Prior | Range | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| \(N_e\) (ancestral) | Log-uniform | \(10^4\)–\(10^5\) | *Rosa* population sizes |
| \(N_e\) (donor) | Log-uniform | \(10^3\)–\(10^4\) | Smaller effective sizes |
| \(t_{hybrid}\) | Log-uniform | 500–5,000 gen | Pre-domestication timeframe |
| \(t_{intro}\) | Log-uniform | 100–2,000 gen | Post-hybridization |
| \(t_{domestication}\) | Log-uniform | 100–500 gen | Historical records |
| \(r\) (recombination) | From LDhat/ReLERNN | Estimated | Not constant |
| \(f_{clonal}\) | Uniform | 0.9–1.0 | Clonal propagation |
| \(m\) (migration) | Log-uniform | \(10^{-5}\)–\(10^{-3}\) | Introgression rate |
| \(\beta_r\) | From simulation | Calibrated | Reference bias |

### D.4 Summary statistics

| Statistic | Description | Tool |
|---|---|---|
| Block length moments | Mean, variance, skewness | Custom |
| Twisst weights | Topology proportions | Twisst |
| DFOIL/Δ | Directional introgression | DFOIL |
| \(F_{ST}\) | Between ancestry blocks | vcftools |
| Site pattern \(f_d\) | Allele frequency spectrum | Custom |
| SV enrichment | SV density at boundaries | BEDTools |
| LD decay | Within/between blocks | PLINK |

### D.5 ABC-RF workflow

```
Step 1: Define scenarios and priors
        └─ As specified above

Step 2: Simulate training set
        ├─ 10,000 simulations per scenario
        └─ Use fastsimcoal2 or msprime

Step 3: Calculate summary statistics
        └─ For each simulation

Step 4: Train random forest
        ├─ 1,000 trees
        └─ mtry = sqrt(n_stats)

Step 5: Predict on observed data
        ├─ Posterior probability per scenario
        └─ Confusion matrix

Step 6: Scenario selection
        └─ F5: BF > 3 or posterior > 0.66
```

### D.6 Model comparison metrics

| Metric | Definition | Threshold |
|---|---|---|
| Bayes factor | \(P(D|S_i) / P(D|S_j)\) | > 3 |
| Posterior probability | RF probability for best scenario | > 0.66 |
| Classification error | Out-of-bag error rate | < 0.2 |
| Variable importance | Top summary statistics | Report |

### D.7 Reporting

Results will be reported as:

1. **Posterior probabilities** for each scenario
2. **Bayes factors** for pairwise comparisons
3. **Variable importance plots**
4. **Scenario selection decision** (F5 status)
5. **Caveats** for interpretation when F5 is violated

